Alabama,Yes,applies only to pro se claims; specifies dismissal without prejudice,Yes,"case dismissal for failing to pay fees, but courts can authorize fee waivers if no funds for 12 months",Three strikes,limits IFP status; exceptions for imminent danger of serious physical injury or manifest injustice,Yes,applies only to pro se claims,"Ala. Code §§ 14-15-1 through 14-15-10 (""Alabama Prisoner Litigation Reform Act"")."
Kentucky,Yes,even if remedy sought is unavailable; financial sanctions for failing to exhaust,Yes,"full payment required before cases can proceed and case dismissal for failure to pay fees, but courts can authorize fee reductions and waivers if unable to pay or for exceptional circumstances",Three strikes,"limits IFP status; ""strikes"" expire in five years; exceptions for imminent danger of serious physical injury",Yes,,Ky. Rev. Stat § 454.400 to 454.415.
Louisiana,Yes,specifies dismissal without prejudice,Yes,and cases can be paused or dismissed for failure to pay fees,Three strikes,limits IFP status; exceptions for imminent danger of serious physical injury,Yes,,La. Stat. Ann. § 15:1181 et seq.
Michigan,Yes,,Yes,"payment required before cases can proceed, including outstanding fees from previous cases",Three strikes,limits IFP status; exceptions for imminent danger of suffering serious physical injury or suffering conduct; good time or disciplinary credit revocations,Yes,,Mich. Comp. Laws Ann. §§ 600.5501-5531 and 600.2963.
Oklahoma,Yes,also applies to formerly incarcerated people,Yes,case dismissal for failure to pay fees,Three strikes,limits IFP status; exceptions for immediate danger of serious physical injury; good time credit revocation (up to 720 credits),Yes,"and applies to any claims relating to arrest, custody, and detention",Okla. Stat. tit. 57 § 564-566.5.
Oregon,NA,,Yes,but courts can authorize fee deferrals or waivers if no current or future funds,Three strikes,limits IFP status; exceptions for imminent danger of serious physical injury,Yes,but must be able to establish economic damages instead of physical injury,Or. Rev. Stat. §§ 30.642 to 30.650.
Idaho,Yes,provides for dismissal with or without prejudice; exceptions for imminent danger of serious physical injury or no administrative remedy system available,Yes,"case dismissal for failing to pay fees, including outstanding fees from previous cases",Two strikes,limits IFP status; pro se claimants must obtain court permission to file future claims; subject to prison disciplinary detention and loss of privileges,Yes,but damages claims permitted with diagnosis of a severe and disabling mental illness,Idaho Code §§ 19-4201 to -4226; and Idaho Code Ann. § 20-209E; 31-3220A.
Florida,NA,,Yes,,Two strikes,within three years limits IFP status; must obtain court permission to file future claims,Yes,applies only to indigent incarcerated litigants,Fla. Stat. § 57.085.
Arizona,NA,,Yes,,Other,Good time credits revocation (5 days),Yes,"requires ""serious physical injury"" but applies only to people convicted of felony offenses","AZ Rev. Stat. Ann. §§ 12-302, 31-201.01(L), and 41-1604.07(L)."
