Arkansas,Yes,,Yes,but waiver permitted,Three strikes,limits IFP status; exceptions for imminent danger of serious physical injury; good time credits revocation (up to 30 days),NA,,"Ark. Code § 16-106-301, 16-68-601 – 607, and 16-106-203."
Colorado,Yes,,Yes,,Three strikes,limits IFP status; exceptions for imminent danger of serious physical injury,NA,,"C.R.S.A. § 13-17.5-101 et seq. Also see Adams v. Corr. Corp. of Am., 187 P.3d 1190 (Colo. App. 2008) (exempts cases brought under common law from the exhaustion requirement)."
Delaware,Yes,,Yes,,Three strikes,limits IFP status; exceptions for imminent danger of serious physical injury,NA,,Del. Code Ann.  Title 10 § 8801-8805.
Iowa,Yes,,Yes,"case dismissal for failing to pay outstanding fees, including from previous cases",Three strikes,limits IFP status; good time credits revocation or debit inmate account,NA,,"Iowa Code § 610A.1, and 610A.3."
Maryland,Yes,specifies dismissal without prejudice if claim does not include proof of exhaustion,Yes,"full payment required before cases can proceed, but courts can authorize fee reductions and waivers",Three strikes,limits IFP status; must obtain court permission to file future claims,NA,,"Md Cts. and Jud. Proc. Code, § 5-1003, 5-1002, and 5-1005."
Mississippi,Yes,but courts can stay proceedings up to 90 days,Yes,,Three strikes,limits IFP status; exceptions for imminent danger of serious physical injury; good time credit revocation for each strike (60 days),NA,,"Miss. Code Ann. §§ 47-5-801-807, 47-5-76, and 47-5-138(3)."
Ohio,Yes,but courts can stay proceedings for 180 days,Yes,remaining fees are added to debt after release,Three strikes,"After within 12 months, court must review each future claim",NA,,"Ohio Rev. Code Ann. §§ 2323.5 1, 2969.21-.27."
Tennessee,Yes,but courts can stay proceedings for 90 days; must file claim within 31 days of exhaustion,Yes,payment required for outstanding fees from previous cases before new cases can proceed,Three strikes,limits IFP status; exception for imminent danger of serious physical injury,NA,,"Tenn. Code Ann. §§ 41-21-801 to -812 (1996). Compare Clifton v. Carpenter, 775 F.3d 760 (6th Cir. 2014) (holding the prohibition unconstitutional as applied to a person on parole facing revocation) with Hughes v. Tennessee Board of Probation and Parole, 514 S.W.3d 707 (Tenn. 2017) (limiting Clifton to its facts)."
Virginia,Yes,,Yes,case dismissal for failure to pay fees,Three strikes,limits IFP status; exceptions for imminent danger of serious physical injury or manifest injustice,NA,,Va. Code Ann. §§ 8.01-689 through 0697 (Virginia Prisoner Litigation Reform Act); and Va. Code Ann. §§ 8.01-195.3 (item 7).
